# Functional Requirements

## 1. Hero KPI Section

Displayed above the fold.

KPI cards must only render when their value is available from fetched public sources for the selected year. Do not show homepage-derived metrics for historical years unless the selected year has a matching public source value.

### KPI Card 1

Top Region

Example:

- Middle East
- Derived from GMTI CSV rows and CLDR regions

Visual treatment:

- Largest card
- Bold typography
- Occupies most visual attention

---

### KPI Card 2

Muslim Traveler Arrivals

Example:

- 186M travelers
- 2025 estimate

Visual treatment:

- Medium-sized card
- Only shown when available for the selected year

---

### KPI Card 3

Market Value

Example:

- USD 225B

Visual treatment:

- Only shown when available for the selected year

---

## 2. Interactive GMTI Score Chart

### Objective

Show GMTI destination score distribution across the currently visible destination ranks.

### Chart Type

Interactive line chart

X-axis:

- Destination rank order

Y-axis:

- GMTI score

Features:

- Hover tooltip
- Responsive layout
- Smooth animation
- Must use numeric score values parsed from the selected GMTI CSV
- Must render an unavailable state when score data is missing or non-numeric

---

## 3. Muslim-Friendly Destinations

Display as ranked cards.

Users must be able to choose how many destinations to view:

- Top 5
- Top 10
- Top 25
- Top 50
- Top 100
- All

The full fetched CSV should remain available in memory so the UI can switch Top N without refetching.

Each destination card includes:

- Rank
- Country name
- GMTI score
- Region
- Rank change
- Source year label, for example `GMTI 2025 CSV`

---

## 4. Regional Market Distribution

Chart Type:

Interactive bar chart

Metrics:

- Asia-Pacific
- Middle East
- Europe
- Africa
- Americas

Display:

- Share of visible destination rows by derived region
- Hover details
- Percent labels must never be clipped or hidden outside the chart bounds
- Regional share and Top Region must update when the user changes Top N

---

## 5. Data Source Section

Display:

"Live data trace"

Table columns:

- Data
- Status
- Live source
- Source URL

Purpose:

- Build trust
- Reduce hallucination concerns
- Show exactly which fetched fields are available or unavailable
- Source links should display as `Open`, including when multiple source links are present
- Do not show an additional source list below the trace table

