# Acceptance Criteria

The solution is accepted when:

✓ Dashboard loads successfully
✓ KPI stat cards display only when values are available for the selected year
✓ At least 1 interactive chart implemented
✓ Destination section supports Top 5, Top 10, Top 25, Top 50, Top 100, and All
✓ Score chart, regional share, and Top Region are based on the selected year and selected Top N
✓ Live data trace table clearly references available and unavailable fields
✓ Responsive on desktop and mobile
✓ Most important available metric visible immediately
✓ Deployable through Vercel, Netlify, GitHub Pages, or equivalent
✓ Data realtime based on Primary Sources
✓ Next.js project structure is cleanly separated into `app`, `lib`, and `components`
✓ Missing fetched data renders as `-` or an unavailable state, not fallback/sample values
✓ Percent labels and chart text are not clipped on desktop or mobile
✓ Loading state uses a polished skeleton/shimmer view while server data is fetched

